nce risk in post-war German history. The firewall is fracturing from both major coalition parties simultaneously. Merz's 13–16% approval (worst-ever for an incumbent chancellor) and the coalition's 34% combined polling (down 11 points since February 2025) mean Germany is attempting to execute its most ambitious external posture — NATO leadership, EU institutional innovation, Ukraine security partnership — on the weakest domestic legitimacy base in the Federal Republic's history. Germany's central structural paradox, identified in prior weeks, has reached its sharpest form: the state's external ambitions (NATO 3.0, associate EU membership, Ukraine drone partnership, UNSC candidacy) are more actively pursued than at any prior point, while the domestic base for sustaining them (coalition cohesion, fiscal delivery capacity, public legitimacy, AfD containment) continues to erode on every axis.",
